+# CVE-2026-73089 — False Positive Assessment for browserslist@4.7.0
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2026-73089 does not affect browserslist 4.7.0.**
+The unbounded query-result `cache` / `parseCache` objects in `index.js` were introduced in 4.7.2. 4.7.0 has no such cache. There is nothing to patch.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+Prior to 4.28.7, `index.js` retains every distinct `(queries, context)` result in `cache` and every `parseQueries()` AST in `parseCache` without a size cap, TTL, or eviction. An attacker who can influence repeated `browserslist()` query values can cause linear memory growth and an out-of-memory crash.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2026-73089
+- **GHSA:** GHSA-c83g-rgw3-j3cx
+- **CWE:** CWE-770
+- **Severity:** High (CVSS 7.5)
+- **Upstream fix commit:** `f2931a3ff2a3a31abf84ef01a7400b270aad6405` — Fix unbounded memory growth
+- **Fixed version:** 4.28.7
+
+---
+
+## Affected Package
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Ecosystem | npm |
+| Package | browserslist |
+| This version | 4.7.0 |
+| Scanner range | < 4.28.7 (introduced: 0) |
+
+---
+
+## Root Cause of the CVE
+
+```js
+var cache = {}
+var parseCache = {}
+if (cache[cacheKey]) return cache[cacheKey]
+cache[cacheKey] = result
+```
+
+The GHSA states this is **not** `node.js` `filenessCache` / `configCache`. Those filesystem caches are a different subsystem and were not the subject of `f2931a3`.
+
+---
+
+## Why 4.7.0 Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. The vulnerable cache was introduced in the next patch release
+
+Commit `2fee1e4` (2019-10-22) added query-result caching. First containing tag: **4.7.2**. 4.7.0 does not include that commit.
+
+### 2. Direct code verification
+
+```
+$ grep -n "var cache =\|var parseCache =\|cache\[cacheKey\]" index.js
+(no output)
+```
+
+4.7.0 `index.js` has no `JSON.stringify([queries, context])` cache key and no `cache[cacheKey] = result`. `node.js` still has only `filenessCache` / `configCache`.
+
+### 3. CVE-2026-73088 is a separate issue and is real on 4.7.0
+
+4.7.0 **does** contain the inlined `getStat()` `var normalized` loop. That is CVE-2026-73088 and is patched in `patch/CVE-2026-73088/`. This dummy is only for CVE-2026-73089.
+
+### 4. Advisory range is overly broad
+
+OSV lists 4.7.0 because the git event range is `introduced: 0`. The unbounded query cache does not exist until 4.7.2.
+
+---
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Date | Event |
+|---|---|
+| 4.7.0 | No query-result cache |
+| 2019-10-22 | `2fee1e4` adds unbounded `cache` (4.7.2) |
+| 2025-01-08 | `1b999cb` adds `parseCache` (4.24.5) |
+| 2026-07-21 | `f2931a3` converts caches to Maps capped at 500 |
+| 2026-08-11 | CVE-2026-73089 published as < 4.28.7 |
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-73089 is a false positive for browserslist@4.7.0.**
+
+No functional source patch is applicable. Scanner findings should be suppressed. (CVE-2026-73088 remains a real backport on this version.)
+
